{
  "description": "Conformance cases for the reader of the attach line: direction attached is the owner reading the first line of an events endpoint (Go ParseVoiceControlPipeAttached, Rust parse_attached). Each case is one line, given by line (text), line_hex (bytes) or line_file (a file under this directory holding the line with no line feed). want.result is accept (with the kind read) or refuse (with the code; the id is always 0, since the line has none). The refusals come in the reader's order: too_long, malformed, unknown_schema (a v1 hello arriving first included), invalid (kind or nonce missing, null, of the wrong type, empty, or a nonce that is not 43 characters of canonical unpadded base64url), unknown_kind (a kind other than attached, once the nonce is well-formed). The golden nonce is this directory's fake secret (sensitive.json); a case holding it shows nothing real.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "attached",
      "direction": "attached",
      "line": "{\"schema\":\"conch.voice_control_pipe.v1\",\"kind\":\"attached\",\"nonce\":\"FAKE_nonce_do_not_print_0123456789abcdefghA\"}",
      "want": {
        "result": "accept",
        "kind": "attached"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "white space around the object, carriage return included",
      "direction": "attached",
      "line": " \t{\"schema\":\"conch.voice_control_pipe.v1\",\"kind\":\"attached\",\"nonce\":\"FAKE_nonce_do_not_print_0123456789abcdefghA\"} \r",
      "want": {
        "result": "accept",
        "kind": "attached"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "the fields in another order",
